+// short multi-token passes such as a speculative verify pass (M = 2..16).
+//
+// Row invariance: a row gets the same bits for every M (verified on the
+// Apple M5 only, see below).
+//   - One pipeline serves every M (M is a uniform, not in the cache key).
+//   - Every row of the tile runs its own inlined copy of the same helper
+//     functions: row_sums (per B word) and store_row (lane sums to workgroup
+//     memory), called once per row with that row's A offset and that row's
+//     own accumulator. A row's sums never depend on the other rows or on M;
+//     rows past M are skipped by uniform branches.
+//   - The copies are separate instructions. Metal compiles WebGPU shaders in
+//     relaxed math mode, which may reassociate float sums, so in principle
+//     two copies could round differently. The op check
